Let me analyze the Yemora language reference carefully and write solutions for each task.

Key points:
- `Trepiho x := <expr>;` declares variable
- `Rashar <expr>;` prints with newline
- `Rurmopa <expr>;` prints without newline
- Functions: `Ruyoyo name(params) ... Opa`
- `Omel <expr>;` returns (expression optional)
- Conditionals: `Mushu <cond> Yeshil Hupo ... Tho Thotri Hupo ... Tho`
- Loops: `Rokomi (cond) {...}`, `Hemorhor {...} Rokomi (cond);`, `Pil (init; cond; update) {...}`
- `Kiyetrel` = break, `Tril` = continue
- Builtins: `Purmo` (length), `Theki` (append), `Mitrer` (to string), `Eshiyer` (string to int), `Thoke` (read line)
- String concat with `+` if either operand is string
- Integer division rounds toward zero, `%` follows
- Comparison `=`, `~=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`
- Logical: `Pethe` (and), `Hiyikra` (or), `Shurisho` (not)
- Lists: `[1,2,3]`, shared, `xs[i]` indexing, `Theki(xs, v)` appends
- `Pakru Sher <expr> Sher lit1, lit2 ... Tho Pakru` switch
- Booleans only as conditions

Now tasks:

### t0-count
Read n, print 1..n one per line. If n=0 print nothing.
```
Trepiho n := Eshiyer(Thoke());
Pil (Trepiho i := 1; i <= n; i := i + 1) {
    Rashar i;
}
```
Simple.

### t0-day-names
Read lines until EOF, for each print day name or invalid.
```
Trepiho line := Thoke();
Rokomi (line ~= Krupelro) {
    Trepiho n := Eshiyer(line);
    Pakru Sher n
    Sher 1
        Rashar "Monday";
    Sher 2
        Rashar "Tuesday";
    ...
    Sher Thotri
        Rashar "invalid";
    Tho Pakru
    line := Thoke();
}
```
Need to check: `Pakru Sher <expression>` - the literal cases. `Sher 2` etc. Fine.

Alternatively use if-else. Switch is cleaner.

Note: Eshiyer handles surrounding spaces. The input lines hold integers. Fine.

### t0-even-odd
Count even/odd, handle negatives. Even check: `n % 2 = 0`. For negative, `-7 % 2` is `-1` per reference (sign follows from rounding toward zero: `-7 - 2*(-3) = -7 + 6 = -1`). So `-7 % 2 = -1`, not 0, correctly odd. `-4 % 2 = -4 - 2*(-2) = 0`, even. So `n % 2 = 0` works for negatives too. 

```
Trepiho evens := 0;
Trepiho odds := 0;
Trepiho line := Thoke();
Rokomi (line ~= Krupelro) {
    Trepiho n := Eshiyer(line);
    Mushu n % 2 = 0 Yeshil Hupo
        evens := evens + 1;
    Tho Thotri Hupo
        odds := odds + 1;
    Tho
    line := Thoke();
}
Rashar "even " + evens;
Rashar "odd " + odds;
```

### t0-factorial
n 0..20, n! up to 20! = 2432902008176640000 which exceeds 64-bit signed max (9223372036854775807 ~9.2e18). 20! = 2.43e18 < 9.2e18, fits in 64-bit. Good.

Recursive or iterative. Let me do iterative to avoid recursion depth concerns (20 fine either way).
```
Trepiho n := Eshiyer(Thoke());
Trepiho result := 1;
Pil (Trepiho i := 1; i <= n; i := i + 1) {
    result := result * i;
}
Rashar result;
```
0! = 1 since loop doesn't execute (1 <= 0 false), result stays 1. Good.

### t0-fizzbuzz
