### t0-reverse-lines
Read all lines, store in list, print reverse.
```
Trepiho lines := [];
Trepiho line := Thoke();
Rokomi (line ~= Krupelro) {
    Theki(lines, line);
    line := Thoke();
}
Pil (Trepiho i := Purmo(lines) - 1; i >= 0; i := i - 1) {
    Rashar lines[i];
}
```
Careful: when input is empty, Thoke() returns Krupelro immediately, lines = [], loop prints nothing. For loop: i := -1, condition -1 >= 0 false. Good.

Lists can mix types but we only add strings. Good.

