One concern: in Yemora, is `i % 15 = 0` okay? Precedence: `%` tighter than comparison `=`. Comparison tighter than Pethe. So `i % 15 = 0` parses as `(i % 15) = 0`. Good. Condition must be boolean - result of `=` is boolean. Good.

Negative modulo for even-odd: confirmed works.

